      "loader_handoff": {
        "address": 68332,
        "basis": "The X-T4 2.12 loader passes its 0x5d0-byte boot-information block in r1 from 0x10aec; the kernel copies it to 0x82adc. Words 0x00..0x3c are the sixteen GPIO port levels the loader samples at power-on and equal the declared GPIO input. The four flash setup words, ending with the NOR manufacturer byte 0x2c, match that copy in RAM read from a running X-T4 2.12. The cold boot reason and every other word stay synthetic.",
