            ]
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "basis": "Declared catalog input.",
          "level": "low",
          "stabilizer_link": {
            "basis": "In-body stabilizer controller on SPI2, as its link behaves: the camera powers it with GPIO outputs 0.12 and 1.14 (powered while both are high), pulses its reset on 12.6 (high, then low releases it), selects it with 12.3 (active low) and exchanges four-byte frames of eight-bit words, most significant first. The controller reports on pad 0.4, which reads its GPIO input level (high) while the controller is unpowered or held in reset: the pad goes low once the controller has booted and high after the first frame of the link. The boot delay, 10 ms at 54 MHz, is declared, not measured. No command reply data is declared, so every reply carries data 0, which the periodic status traffic at the shooting screen (status id 0x29 every 40 ms, ids 0x2a and 0x11a) accepts.",
